What is an API?
# API stands for Application Programming Interface.
# It is a software interface which allows two or more computer programs to communicate with each other.
# It's a set of rules or protocols that define how applications communicate with each other using requests or responses.

Why are APIs being used?
# It can access data from other systems.
# Connect different applications and share functionality without exposing the source code.
# Common APIs are:- Google Maps API, GitHub API, OpenWeather API.

What are the ways to call an API?
# XMLHttp Request:- This is the oldest way and is also a bit complex in the way.    https://javascript.info/xmlhttprequest
# Fetch API:- This is the new method and is easier to use compared to the XMLHttp Request.

FETCH API:-
# This method uses the fetch(url,options) method to call the API.
url → API endpoint(link of API)
options → Optional settings like method, headers, body, etc.
# fetch() is a built-in JavaScript function used to send HTTP requests to a server and receive data from it.
# You'll be getting a promise once the request is being fetched.
# Inorder to collect the data from the promise fetched you can follow the steps below:-
~ Use a then method: a response will be printed in the body part which will be in JSON format and this will not be in the readable format.
  To get the JSON we'll have to use the response.json().
~ response.json() is used to convert the json format into a Javascript object.
To be clear at first we'll be using a fetch() and will be receiving the promise. To fetech the data from the promise we'll be using a .then() and will be receiving a JSON format output.
To get the data from the JSON output we'll be using the response.json() to receive a promise.
Atlast we'll be using the .then() to get the actual data from the API.

fetch('https://poetrydb.org/author')  //fetched data
.then(function(response) {           //used then() to  fetch the promise
   return response.json()            //used response.json() to receive the promise
})
    .then(function(data) {           //used the .then() to retrieve the data in the API
        console.log(data)
    })

PROMISE:-
# A promise is a JavaScript object that represents the eventual completion or failure of an asynchronous operation.
# It has three states:- Pending, Fulfilled(Settled) and Rejected.
# Pending if the taks is still running, fulfilled if you get the correct response or the task is completed successfully and rejected if the task is failed.
# .then() is used to run when a promise is successfull and .catch() is used to run when a promise is failed.

How to handle errors in Promises?
# Settled promises will be either fulfilled or rejected and when an error occurs the promises will be rejected.
# To run the code when the promise gets rejected, we can use the use.catch() method.
# We'll be able to use the catch() method so that the page will not be crashed fully and you'll be able to display the error message on the console.
.catch(function(error) {
        console.log(error)
    })

What is a JSON format?
# JSON stands for JavaScript Object Notation. It is the standard ir light-weight format of data that is being used to store and exchange data between client-server communication.
# It is self-describing and is easy to use. In JSON, keys must be inside double quotes followed by the values and is written inside curly braces.
# The data types supported for JSON format are:- String, Number, Boolean, Null, Object, Array.
# JSON.stringify() is a JavaScript method that converts a JavaScript object into a JSON string.
# JSON.parse() is a JavaScript method that converts a JSON string into a JavaScript Object.
const student = { 
    name : "Ajay",
    age : 28 ,
    employee : true
}
const jsonObj = JSON.stringify(student)
console.log(jsonObj)

const jsonO = JSON.parse(jsonObj)
console.log(jsonO)

What is a WebSpeech API?
# WebSpeech API is a JavaScript API that allows web applications for speech synthesis and speech recognition. The two main components are:-
 ~ Convert speech to text (Speech Recognition)
 ~ Convert text to speech (Speech Synthesis)
# It is supported by Chrome, Edhe and Firefox.
SPEECH RECOGNITION:-
# It is a technology that uses the microphonee to listen to a user's voice and converts it into text.
# The key methods/events in this are:-
 ~ SpeechRecognition(): This initializes the speech recognition engine.
 ~ start() and stop()
 ~ onresult: This event captures the spoken words and gives you the spoken text.
